Let's go tear it up.

71
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,941
Just in time for us to celebrate.

72
00:03:54,140 --> 00:03:57,080
I'm about to let loose, baby. Yeah!

73
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,020
It's festival time!

74
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,320
We're ready to party!

75
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,471
This is going to be a disaster, I know it.

76
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:12,480
Add cloudier mushrooms and chrysanthemum
leaves, a plate of Geoise tofu,

77
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:16,840
some flower-shaped lotus
roots, next up, cucumber salad.

78
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:20,460
We must not let any harm
befall our honored guests.

79
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:23,860
Grind everything once,
heat it up and reshape it?

80
00:04:24,020 --> 00:04:26,200
then test it for poison three times.

81
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:30,837
I've honed these skills over decades,
all in service of this wondrous day.

82
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:33,220
Traditional cuisine fit for a shogun!

83
00:04:34,500 --> 00:04:35,600
Please enjoy!

84
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:37,580
What is this?

85
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:38,779
Where is everyone?

86
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,320
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

87
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:44,525
A rowdy crew won't wait two hours
for food, no matter how tasty.

88
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:47,544
A pity, since this is
quite the sight to behold.

89
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,622
You've done splendid work, Chef.

90
00:04:50,080 --> 00:04:50,910
Hm?

91
00:04:50,993 --> 00:04:53,234
It sounds like the festival's starting.

92
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,200
Party time! Party time!

93
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:58,107
Let's grab that food and go!

94
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:00,860
Chocolate bananas!

95
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:02,260
Fried noodles!

96
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:03,557
Octopus balls!

97
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:04,940
Wow, squid!

98
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:06,420
That's candy, too!

99
00:05:11,220 --> 00:05:12,740
This is the greatest!

100
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:14,170
That festival?

101
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:15,257
Everything's free!

102
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:16,400
Totally free!

103
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:18,880
My very first festival!

104
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,360
This is so fun!

105
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,397
I can't decide what I want to eat next!

106
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:25,237
There's just so much
awesome-looking stuff, you know?

107
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:27,700
Hey, look over there! What are those?

108
00:05:27,940 --> 00:05:29,477
They're called candy apples!

109
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:30,390
You eat it?

110
00:05:30,473 --> 00:05:31,494
It looks like a jewel!

111
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:33,210
Beautiful!

112
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:41,380
It's sweet and sour and delicious.

113
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:44,677
Fruit is good, but candy
fruit is a dream come true.

114
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:47,172
Okay, less talking, more eating, Chopper.

115
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:53,220
Now that's tasty!

116
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:58,077
There's stalls with games
and stuff too, right?

117
00:05:58,160 --> 00:06:00,977
Since you guys are the festival
experts, can you show me some?

118
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:02,617
No, bro, follow me.

119
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:06,759
Once you've had all the food, there's
one thing you always gotta try!

120
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:11,020
Right now! Gum-Gum! Target! Shoot it!

121
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:13,880
I never miss!

122
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:17,497
I don't think that's how you play!

123
00:06:17,580 --> 00:06:19,477
Yeah, Luffy, you can't use your hand!

124
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,390
Oh, okay!

125
00:06:20,473 --> 00:06:21,361
Can I try again?

126
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:27,660
I broke the net!

127
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:28,980
You're up next!

128
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:31,612
Don't worry, I'll show you how it's done!

129
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:40,500
Two in one stroke!

130
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:42,213
Wow, you're a real pro!

131
00:06:42,420 --> 00:06:44,302
Oh, I wish I was as good as you!

132
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:48,899
That sweet time doesn't
make me happy, you bastards!

133
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,700
Looks pretty happy to me!

134
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,380
All right, Wano!

135
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,400
You wanna rock?

136
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:00,700
Hey, it's Brook!

137
00:07:01,060 --> 00:07:02,940
Knock him down, Brook! Yeah!

138
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:06,244
I'd like to introduce you
all to my jam partner!

139
00:07:07,380 --> 00:07:09,280
Wano's Pitch Perfect Princess!

140
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:12,577
Cause if you rock with the Soul
King, then you gotta be royalty!

141
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:13,490
That's right!

142
00:07:13,620 --> 00:07:16,326
We're serving up Brother
Omer's favorite tune!

143
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:18,100
Moon Princess!

144
00:07:20,740 --> 00:07:21,940
Princess Yachty!

145
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,437
What are these?

146
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:40,197
Find something of interest. Nico Robin.

147
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:41,957
Mr. Tang.

148
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:42,897
You know my name?

149
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:44,877
What do you think of my treasure?

150
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:46,937
What aren't they cute?

151
00:07:47,020 --> 00:07:49,557
They're fine.

152
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:53,197
I struck a nerve.

153
00:07:53,280 --> 00:07:55,277
You're funny. Mr. Tang.

154
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:59,740
By the way, this is a rather odd
place for your collection. Isn't it?

155
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:03,080
I do hope you realize I was joking.

156
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:06,277
I suppose you might call
this my secret hobby room,

157
00:08:06,360 --> 00:08:09,280
and I was also confined
here for quite some time.

158
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:12,730
Confined?

159
00:08:12,813 --> 00:08:15,008
It seems you're more
than just a swordsmith.

160
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:17,480
Yes, it's but a pastime.

161
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:20,368
Seems I have a good
aptitude for it, though.

162
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:28,708
I never cared for
festivals during my reign.

163
00:08:29,340 --> 00:08:31,160
Wait, who are you really?

164
00:08:31,860 --> 00:08:33,580
Ah, well...

165
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:40,960
I am the father of Kozuki Oden.

166
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:43,720
My name is Kozuki Sukiyaki.

167
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,300
The Shogun?

168
00:08:45,540 --> 00:08:47,280
Does Momo know you're alive?

169
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:48,830
He doesn't.

170
00:08:48,913 --> 00:08:50,289
And I'll keep it that way.

171
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:54,694
But I have a feeling my son's retainers
have figured out who I am by now.

172
00:08:55,440 --> 00:09:00,040
At any rate, I'm the one responsible
for the tragedy that befell this land.

173
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:04,600
I'm too ashamed to tell
anyone that I'm alive.

174
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:07,245
When I emerged from this room,

175
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:11,940
barely clinging to life, Odin was
dead and my beloved home was in ruins.

176
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:15,040
I felt such remorse.

177
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:17,574
I thought to slip my belly on the spot.

178
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:21,760
Still, I had no choice but to hide.

179
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:24,066
I had a mission to carry out.

180
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,620
I could not fail my country again.

181
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:29,810
But now,

182
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:31,217
the land of Wano is free,

183
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:35,260
and for that I owe my deepest
gratitude to you and your friends.

184
00:09:36,360 --> 00:09:40,301
Well, I think they'd be very happy
if you told them that in person.

185
00:09:40,940 --> 00:09:41,770
I see.

186
00:09:43,180 --> 00:09:46,651
That aside, there's something
else I need to ask you about.

187
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:50,217
I've been informed that this
country has an ancient weapon.

188
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:51,130
Pluton.

189
00:09:57,200 --> 00:10:02,440
How did you know that it's written on
the poneglyph in the kingdom of Alabasta?

190
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:10,960
I never imagined you'd know of
such a thing but yes it's here!

191
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:26,720
Oh, I've got my voluptuous car!

192
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:28,840
You don't know when to quit!

193
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:30,877
You guys aren't even captains.

194
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:33,607
If I lose to you, I'll
be a walking discreet!

195
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:37,897
This is a damn mess, and the Navy
doesn't have the manpower to clean it up.

196
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:40,877
But it looks like you were
worth fighting after all.

197
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:43,548
Wouldn't want you to
start in trouble later.

198
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:54,380
This is weak booze if I've ever tasted it.

199
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:57,952
Should have expected that from
a weak-ass crew like yours.

200
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:02,110
Hello?

201
00:11:02,193 --> 00:11:03,023
This is...

202
00:11:03,106 --> 00:11:03,936
Listen, it's me.

203
00:11:04,019 --> 00:11:07,380
Send a warship to the land
of Wano. What? Real kugyu?

204
00:11:07,660 --> 00:11:10,960
And don't squeal the sakazuki
either, got it? Kullik.

205
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:14,720
No offense, boss.

206
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:15,920
I still like you.

207
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:19,452
Especially the way you never cut corners.

208
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:25,820
If I break some rules,
I know you won't mind.

209
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:29,072
Because I'm bringing you this kid's head.

210
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:35,980
Look, up there! Who is that?

211
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:40,180
Time for a toast, I see!

212
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:42,306
Is he going to make a speech?

213
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:45,739
Ninja's pirates, minx, and samurai!

214
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:47,500
The shogun's retainers!

215
00:11:47,700 --> 00:11:49,437
Yakuza and the people of Wano!

216
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:52,377
You guys really kicked some ass out there!

217
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:53,520
You said it, pal!

218
00:11:53,620 --> 00:11:54,537
Whoever you are!

219
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:55,740
I'll drink to that!

220
00:11:55,880 --> 00:11:58,400
This guy's the king of the banquet! Yeah!

221
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,132
I'm king of the banquet!

222
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:02,350
Muffy.

223
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:06,700
Don't tell the land of
Wano about me, okay?

224
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:08,560
What? Why not?

225
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:10,377
Because it'd make me a hero.

226
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:11,857
And what's wrong with that?

227
00:12:11,940 --> 00:12:13,737
You're the one who defeated Kaido.

228
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:15,097
The people need to know.

229
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:16,040
Don't be dumb.

230
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:18,940
Wano has been waiting
for you, Momo, not me.

231
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:22,020
Get out of my body!

232
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,660
Hey, straw hatch! Huh?

233
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:27,940
I'm taking you out right now! Taggy!

234
00:12:28,140 --> 00:12:30,260
Fireworks ready? Let's go!

235
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:34,460
A toast to good food every single day!

236
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,540
What the hell?

237
00:12:37,660 --> 00:12:38,580
I'll kill you!

238
00:12:41,140 --> 00:12:42,540
Here we go!

239
00:12:43,320 --> 00:12:44,150
Cheers!

240
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:49,770
Yeah!

241
00:12:50,300 --> 00:12:52,317
It's time to show them how to party!

242
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:53,230
Yeah!

243
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:02,340
Hmm, perhaps another bottle is in order.

244
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:04,400
Time for a feast!

245
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:07,180
Empty those cups and fill them up again!

246
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,040
Don't stop till dawn!

247
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:13,220
Pirates know how to
celebrate, I'll say that much.

248
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:18,060
In all my futures, I've never
been to a banquet like this.

249
00:13:20,720 --> 00:13:26,320
Listen, this victory, this moment shared
with friends, will stay with me forever.

250
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,917
I'm not here to have a
toast with you, damn it!

251
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,117
And why come to the
party in the first place?

252
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:37,877
Guess you haven't been keeping
up with the news overseas, huh?

253
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:39,060
Here, see this?

254
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:42,082
I'm gonna take you out
while I still have a shot!

255
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:50,130
Wado?!

256
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:55,037
The news that shocked the world came
as quite a surprise to Luffy as well.

257
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:56,857
It was a moment that marked the end of the

258
00:13:56,940 --> 00:13:59,480
old regime and the beginning of a new era.

259
